        "PROLOGUE - THE SLOW LOCK",
        "Author: Long ago, when the kingdoms still believed that every darkness could be defeated by a bright enough sword, a fellowship of four heroes climbed the black steps of Darkstorm Keep. They went to destroy Vharruk Ashmourn, the Demon Lord whose armies had turned the eastern sky red.",
        "Author: Only the four returned, and none of them spoke of victory. They carried a crown divided into three burning fragments, raised four bronze statues on Hero's Overlook, and told the world that Vharruk had been sealed beneath Ashtonia forever.",
        "Author: The seal was praised as a prison. In truth, it was a slow lock. Every passing year loosened one invisible tooth. Every forgotten promise turned the key a little farther.",
        "Author: Seven years passed. Then Darkstorm Keep appeared again on the western headland, although no road had led to it the night before. Two weeks later, Oakheaven stopped sending grain. Last night, ash fell upon Hero's Overlook from a clear and star-filled sky.",
        "Author: This is where the old heroes' story ends. This is where yours begins.",
        "Character Awakening",
        "Author: Morning enters the small room as a thin grey line. Ash has gathered on the windowsill like winter dust. Beneath it lies a sealed letter bearing the lighthouse mark of the Adventurers' Guild.",
        "{user_nickname}: Ash in summer. A Guild seal on my table. Whatever this is, it has already found me.",
        "GAME: Character creation: choose race, class, and distribute +3, +2, +1, +1, +0 among MIGHT, GRACE, WITS, SOUL, and BOND.",
        "Racial Memory",
