        "ACT I - THE CRACKED STATUE",
        "Chapter 1 - Ash at Hero's Overlook",
        "Author: Hero's Overlook stands above the valley on a shelf of white stone. Four bronze heroes face the distant mountains. By tradition, travelers touch the statues for luck. This morning no one approaches them.",
        "Author: The statue at the center has cracked from brow to heart. Black grains drift from the fracture, rising against the wind instead of falling.",
        "Brother Aldwyn: You came. Good. I was afraid the road might change its mind.",
        "{user_nickname}: You were expecting me? We have never met.",
        "Brother Aldwyn: No. But seven years ago, someone told me what you would look like when the ash returned.",
        "Author: The caretaker is old, but his hands are steady. Around his neck hangs a bronze key shaped like a broken crown.",
        "Brother Aldwyn: Take the Guild summons. Go to Misthaven Port. Register. Find out why every expedition sent toward Ashtonia has vanished.",
        "{user_nickname}: And the statue?",
        "Brother Aldwyn: The statue is a warning. If all four break, the thing beneath the mountain will no longer need a door.",
