        "ACT II - THE ADVENTURERS' GUILD",
        "Chapter 3 - The Lighthouse with No Sea-Light",
        "Author: No matter which road you chose, it eventually delivers you to Misthaven Port. The lighthouse windows burn gold above the fog, and the Guild hall below them is crowded with maps, weapons, contracts, and people pretending not to be afraid.",
        "Corvane Ashford: Welcome to the last organized mistake in the western kingdoms.",
        "{user_nickname}: That is not a reassuring description of an Adventurers' Guild.",
        "Corvane Ashford: Reassurance is free. Accurate information is expensive.",
        "Author: Corvane places a contract on the table. It orders you to travel to Oakheaven, determine why its grain caravans stopped, and return with proof. A second page, hidden beneath the first, authorizes a later expedition to Ashtonia.",
        "{user_nickname}: You sent other parties east. None returned.",
