        "ACT III - OAKHEAVEN AND THE UNBURNED TOWN",
        "Chapter 6 - A Town Being Consumed",
        "Author: Oakheaven should smell of wheat, apples, and millwater. Instead it smells of cold smoke. The town has been occupied by demons for eleven days, yet not one house is burned. People sweep their thresholds, open their shops, and greet you with smiles held a second too long.",
        "{user_nickname}: This is not a siege. It is a performance.",
        "Mirelle Ashcroft: Keep your voice low. The mayor has not slept in eleven days, and his shadow moves when he does not.",
        "Author: Mirelle, the mill-keeper's daughter, shows you possession sigils hidden beneath doors. In the orchards, Goblin Lord Kregg the Sundered has camped with a warband. They are not attacking Oakheaven; they are fleeing the demons inside it.",
        "Kregg the Sundered: We steal grain. We break fences. We do not wear people like coats. Today, that makes us the respectable army.",
        "Author: The moral trap becomes clear. You can save the town's buildings or its people quickly, but not both. A slower cure may save nearly everyone while giving Vharruk more time.",
        "The Mage Solution - Burn the Sigils",
