        "Chapter 7 - The Voice Behind the Face",
        "Author: When the final demon is cornered, it does not roar. It smiles with a face you trust.",
        "The Possessed: You are carrying his invitation. Ask Aldwyn why he knew you. Ask Corvane why every road he marks leads closer to the seal.",
        "{user_nickname}: Which one of them serves Vharruk?",
        "The Possessed: The one you will defend when the truth becomes inconvenient.",
        "Author: The demon dissolves into ash, leaving no answer behind. Oakheaven's survivors gather in the square. Their health, courage, and numbers will determine how many stand beside you at the end.",
        "GAME: Set oakheaven_result. Main quest reward: 250 EXP. The second companion slot becomes available at Level 5.",
        "ACT IV - THE GATHERING",
        "Author: The three Crown Fragments lie in three places that disagree with ordinary maps: Ashtonia's sealed furnace, the heart-tree of the Whispering Woods, and the dead halls of Karag-Dur. You may seek them in any order. The Ash Clock punishes hesitation, and every fragment teaches the same truth from a different direction.",
        "Chapter 8 - Ashtonia's Sealed Chamber",
        "Author: Beneath the volcano, a spiral stair descends around a column of fire. Demons kneel facing outward, guarding the chamber from something below rather than protecting it from you.",
        "Karnyx the Greater Demon: At last, the courier arrives.",
        "{user_nickname}: I am no one's courier.",
        "Karnyx: Then why do you carry a contract written before you were born?",
        "Author: The Guild summons burns without being consumed. Invisible writing appears beneath Corvane's seal: \"Deliver the fragments to the old table. Let the fifth choose the debt.\"",
        "PLAYER CHOICE",
        "Fight Karnyx and claim the First Fragment. [MIGHT/GRACE.]",
        "Ask why demons guard the seal from below. [BOND.]",
        "Read the contract's hidden layer. [WITS; confirms the seal is being broken from outside.]",
        "Purify the chamber. [SOUL; corruption -1.]",
        "Revelation: The Crown was never merely a weapon. It is the physical form of a bargain.",
        "Chapter 9 - The Heart-Tree's Fifth Shadow",
        "Author: At the center of the Whispering Woods, four old trees grow around an empty space. Their branches form the outline of a fifth tree that was cut from memory.",
        "Sil'Vaneth: There were not four heroes. There were five. Four statues honor those who resisted. The fifth survived by ensuring no one remembered the bargain.",
        "{user_nickname}: Who was the fifth?",
        "Sil'Vaneth: A name is a door. I will not open it until you decide what you will do with the truth.",
        "Author: A Dread Wraith emerges from the absent tree, carrying the memories of the fellowship's forgotten member.",
        "PLAYER CHOICE",
        "Defeat the Dread Wraith. [Combat; second_fragment=true.]",
        "Restore its name with a Bard's song. [Bard free path.]",
        "Heal the memory instead of destroying it. [Healer path; gain evidence.]",
        "Bind it into the fragment. [Mage path; corruption +1.]",
        "Revelation: The fourth public hero did not seal Vharruk. The hidden fifth negotiated with him.",
        "Chapter 10 - Karag-Dur, Where Nothing Lives",
        "Author: The halls of Karag-Dur are carved with feasts, births, and coronations, but no funerals. Nerath-Dur forbade the dead to leave because he believed the surface world would misuse the Third Fragment.",
        "Nerath-Dur the Lich: You are carrying the contract to the one who signed it.",
        "{user_nickname}: Then tell me the name.",
        "Nerath-Dur: Names without proof become accusations. Proof waits in the Fellowship Vault.",
        "Author: Above, Troll King Grommash-Vurr strikes the great forge with a stolen hammer. He wants a war worthy of being remembered. Below, Ser Halbrecht asks only that the hold be allowed to rest.",
        "Four Doors Through Karag-Dur",
        "PLAYER CHOICE",
        "MAGE - Treat with Nerath-Dur as an equal scholar; trade one cherished memory for the fragment. [corruption +2.]",
        "WARRIOR - Defeat Grommash-Vurr honorably; inherit his warband and storm the crypt. [war_score +2.]",
        "BARD - Learn Nerath-Dur's lament and sing the hold's fall back to him. [The king yields.]",
        "HEALER - Consecrate seven shrines; weaken the Lich until he can surrender the fragment and rest.",
        "Reward: third_fragment=true; access to Karag-Dur's forge; possible companions Grommash-Vurr or Ser Halbrecht.",
        "Chapter 11 - The Traitor's Errand",
        "Author: The final fragment completes the memory. Images pass through your mind: four exhausted heroes, Vharruk behind a wall of fire, and a fifth figure stepping forward with a contract.",
        "Vharruk's Memory: One soul each season, and the world remains safe. Refuse, and I walk free.",
        "Author: Three heroes objected and fell trying to break the terms. The fourth divided the Crown so that no single person could change the contract. The fifth returned home, fed the seal with volunteers, and built a heroic lie around the cost.",
        "{user_nickname}: Every expedition. Every \"missing\" adventurer. They were payments.",
        "Author: The identity of the living traitor depends on your investigation. If you studied the Guild and its altered reports, the signer is Guildmaster Corvane Ashford. If you studied the Overlook, the statues, and Aldwyn's impossible foreknowledge, the signer is Brother Aldwyn. If you ignored both trails, the answer waits at the worst possible moment: the throne room.",
        "GAME: Set traitor. The entire quest has been designed to bring all three fragments and a willing hero to Vharruk, so the bargain can be renewed.",
        "ACT V - THE NINE GATES OF DARKSTORM KEEP",
        "Author: Darkstorm Keep stands on a headland where the storm never moves. Its nine walls overlap like the rings of an enormous lock. Each gate offers four methods: force, guile, ritual, or mercy. Your class makes some paths easier, but no path is morally neutral.",
        "Gate I - The Gate of Rust",
