        "GAME: War Score 12+: the three ancient statues animate and join the battle; Vharruk enters Phase Three already weakened. Score 6-11: a hard but winnable battle. Score 0-5: the hero fights nearly alone and risks permanently losing a companion.",
        "Chapter 15 - Phase One: The Herald",
        "Author: The first shadow reaches the Overlook before Vharruk. Greater Demons fall from the storm like sparks and gather around a horned Herald carrying the seal's broken chain.",
        "The Herald: One fragment for every lie. One hero for every season.",
        "{user_nickname}: The seasons belong to the living.",
        "Author: Allied forces hold the stairs while you seek the summoner. If the Herald falls, the summoned demons lose their path into the world.",
        "GAME: Combat objective: defeat the Herald, protect allies, and prevent three summoning circles from completing.",
        "Chapter 16 - Phase Two: The Contract",
        "Author: Vharruk steps onto the stone table without crossing the distance between. The joined Crown rises from your hands and seals itself around a sphere of black fire. While it remains whole, he cannot be harmed.",
        "Vharruk Ashmourn: Break it, and the lesser demons roam forever. Wear it, and you become my keeper. Bind it, and one of you remains here in my place. Every victory is another name for a cost.",
        "{user_nickname}: Then I will choose the cost you forgot to offer.",
        "FINAL DECISION",
        "BREAK the Crown and end the cycle honestly.",
        "WEAR the Crown and accept the fifth seat.",
        "SING the Sealing Song. [Bard + War Score 6.]",
        "REFORGE the Crown into a door. [Dwarf + all fragments + Karag-Dur forge.]",
        "CARRY the seal through a willing magical bond. [Healer; protective heroic ending.]",
        "GIVE the Crown to the traitor and renew the old world.",
        "Chapter 17 - Phase Three: The Ash",
        "Author: Denied the certainty of the contract, Vharruk abandons his form. He becomes the falling ash itself. The battlefield vanishes beneath a grey storm, and only holy ground, the Sealing Song, or the reforged Crown can hold him still long enough to strike.",
        "Vharruk Ashmourn: You cannot defeat what people are willing to forget.",
        "{user_nickname}: Then we will remember everything.",
        "Author: The four bronze statues turn toward the storm. If your allies are strong enough, three step down from their pedestals. The cracked statue remains still until the traitor chooses a side.",
        "GAME: Final combat objective: create three safe zones, expose Vharruk's core, and resolve the Crown according to the selected ending.",
        "EPILOGUES - THE SEVEN ENDINGS",
        "ENDING I - THE CROWN BROKEN",
        "GAME: Requirement: Destroy the Crown during the finale.",
        "Author: The Crown breaks with a sound smaller than thunder and greater than any bell. Vharruk falls, and the old protection falls with him. Lesser demons remain in distant places, no longer commanded and no longer fed. The world is not perfectly safe, but no hidden contract asks the innocent to pay for that safety. At dawn, {user_nickname} places the final shard on the stone table and tells the gathered survivors the entire truth. It is the honest ending.",
        "ENDING II - THE CROWN WORN",
        "GAME: Requirement: Accept Vharruk's offer.",
        "Author: {user_nickname} takes the fifth seat. Darkstorm Keep becomes a palace instead of a prison. Roads reopen. Crops return. One soul is demanded each season, and the new ruler begins by promising that there will always be another solution before payment is due. Years later, the promise remains; so does the Crown. Companions decide whether to guard the ruler, oppose the ruler, or leave before loyalty becomes obedience.",
        "ENDING III - THE CROWN SUNG",
        "GAME: Requirement: Bard; learn the Sealing Song; War Score 6+.",
        "Author: The Bard does not sing to overpower Vharruk. The song names every person erased by the bargain, and thousands of voices answer. A contract sustained by secrecy cannot survive being remembered. The Crown opens like a flower of dark gold and releases every captive name. Vharruk is sealed without tribute for the first time. No cost. No contract. The hardest ending to reach.",
        "ENDING IV - THE CROWN REFORGED",
        "GAME: Requirement: Dwarf; reach Karag-Dur's forge with all fragments.",
        "Author: At Karag-Dur, the fragments are heated in a fire that burns promises instead of wood. The Dwarf reshapes the Crown into a door. When Vharruk charges, the door opens onto the emptiness beyond his own realm and closes behind him. The contract remains as harmless metal, proof of what happened. This is the rarest ending.",
        "ENDING V - THE CROWN GIVEN",
        "GAME: Requirement: Hand the Crown to the traitor.",
        "Author: The traitor receives the Crown with trembling hands and thanks {user_nickname} sincerely. That is the worst part. The seal is renewed, the ash stops, and celebrations begin before the truth can spread. The campaign ends with the world exactly as it was: safe, grateful, and already preparing the next payment.",
        "ENDING VI - THE CROWN CARRIED",
        "GAME: Requirement: Healer; choose the selfless seal at the stone table.",
        "Author: The Healer places both hands on the stone and draws the corruption out of the land, not into flesh, but into the Crown's empty name. The artifact closes around the darkness and becomes silent. {user_nickname} survives, forever changed but free. The world is genuinely safe. The companions build a fifth statue on the Overlook - not as a tomb, but as a promise that healing can end what power only postpones.",
        "ENDING VII - THE ASH FALLS",
        "GAME: Requirement: Ash Clock reaches 10.",
        "Author: Vharruk emerges before the fragments can be joined. The final battle begins wherever {user_nickname} stands. Allies arrive too late or not at all, and victory becomes impossible to make clean. Yet resistance still matters: civilians escape, companions carry the truth away, and Vharruk is wounded deeply enough that another story may one day finish this one. Losing here is real, but it is not meaningless.",
        "Final Image",
        "Author: Every ending closes on the same image. Dawn reaches Hero's Overlook. Four bronze statues face the valley, and the cracked place among them catches the first light. The caretaker sweeps ash from the stone table. Somewhere below, people begin telling the story again - this time with every name included.",
        "{user_nickname}: If a story can become a prison, then perhaps the truth can become a key.",
        "QUEST BOOK - MAIN AND SIDE QUESTS",
        "Author: The journey is organized around Main Quests that advance the central story and Side Quests that reveal the world, recruit allies, recover equipment, and provide additional combat experience. Monsters also grant EXP when defeated. The player may therefore gain levels through a mixture of story progress, exploration, and battle.",
        "GAME: At every level-up, the player receives 3 Skill Points. Skill selection and the Skill Tree are handled by the separate skill system and are intentionally not defined in this scenario.",
