        "Demon Lord Vharruk",
        "Story finale; EXP is replaced by the chosen ending",
        "GAME: EXP is granted once per encounter, not once per summoned creature. Enemies created repeatedly by the same summoner give no additional EXP. This prevents farming while keeping combat rewarding.",
        "MAIN QUEST CHAIN",
        "MQ-01 - Ash on the Overlook",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 1. Quest giver: Brother Aldwyn.",
        "Author: Inspect the cracked statue, receive the Guild summons, and decide whether to trust Aldwyn.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Optional Wraith encounter beneath the statue.",
        "REWARD: 100 EXP; Guild Summons; trust flag.",
        "MQ-02 - The Road That Is Yours",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 1-2. Quest giver: Racial route.",
        "Author: Follow the Elf, Orc, Human, or Dwarf opening and discover the first evidence connected to the Crown.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Goblin patrol, Skeletons, Demons, or Phantoms according to route.",
        "REWARD: 120 EXP; regional ally or early fragment opportunity.",
        "MQ-03 - The Lighthouse Guild",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 2. Quest giver: Guildmaster Corvane.",
        "Author: Reach Misthaven Port, complete the class registration trial, and sign the Oakheaven contract.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Class trial; optional arena fight for Warriors.",
        "REWARD: 150 EXP; Guild rank; first companion slot.",
        "MQ-04 - Pages That Should Be Missing",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 3. Quest giver: Chosen companion.",
        "Author: Enter the Guild archive and recover the altered expedition report without losing the evidence.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Guild guards can be avoided; a possessed archivist becomes a Wraith if exposed.",
        "REWARD: 140 EXP; investigation_evidence +1.",
        "MQ-05 - The Silent Grain Road",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 3-4. Quest giver: Corvane Ashford.",
        "Author: Travel from Misthaven to Oakheaven, inspect the abandoned caravans, and keep at least one survivor alive.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Hobgoblins, Slimes in the flooded road, one Demon scout.",
        "REWARD: 180 EXP; supplies; Oakheaven entry route.",
        "MQ-06 - The Unburned Town",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 4-5. Quest giver: Mirelle Ashcroft.",
        "Author: Discover the possession network and choose the Mage, Warrior, Bard, or Healer solution for Oakheaven.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Possessed townsfolk, Demons, Greater Demon mayor; non-combat solutions remain possible.",
        "REWARD: 250 EXP; oakheaven_result; militia 0-3 War Score.",
        "MQ-07 - The First Crown Fragment",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 4-6. Quest giver: Open objective.",
        "Author: Recover whichever Crown Fragment the player chooses first.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Regional Tier-2 monsters and one elite guardian.",
        "REWARD: 220 EXP; first_fragment; +1 investigation clue.",
        "MQ-08 - The Second Crown Fragment",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 6-7. Quest giver: Open objective.",
        "Author: Reach a second fragment location and resolve its guardian's moral demand.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Greater Demon, Dread Wraith, Troll King, or Lich depending on order.",
        "REWARD: 260 EXP; second_fragment; companion loyalty opportunity.",
        "MQ-09 - The Third Crown Fragment",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 7-8. Quest giver: Open objective.",
        "Author: Claim the final fragment and survive the memory released when the Crown becomes complete.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Tier-3 regional boss and the Echo of the Fifth Hero.",
        "REWARD: 320 EXP; third_fragment; traitor evidence completed.",
        "MQ-10 - The Traitor's Errand",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 8. Quest giver: Story revelation.",
        "Author: Compare the evidence from Aldwyn, Corvane, the Guild records, and the fragments; identify the living traitor.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Optional battle against an Ash Doppelganger copying the suspected traitor.",
        "REWARD: 220 EXP; traitor set; hidden route into Darkstorm Keep.",
        "MQ-11 - The Nine Gates",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 8-9. Quest giver: Darkstorm Keep.",
        "Author: Pass all nine gates by force, guile, ritual, or mercy. Every third gate creates a checkpoint.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Skeleton Knights, Phantoms, King Slime, Warrior Trolls, Dread Wraith, Chimeras, Greater Demons.",
        "REWARD: 40 EXP per gate; 180 EXP completion bonus; Fellowship Vault access.",
        "MQ-12 - The Fifth Pedestal",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 9. Quest giver: The traitor.",
        "Author: Open the Fellowship Vault, read the original contract, and decide what to do with the traitor.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Living memories of the fallen fellowship; avoidable boss encounter.",
        "REWARD: 250 EXP; ending routes unlocked.",
        "MQ-13 - The Crown's Real Offer",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 9. Quest giver: Vharruk Ashmourn.",
        "Author: Enter the throne room, hear Vharruk's offer, and escape Darkstorm Keep with the joined Crown.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Vharruk's projection; pursuit by Greater Demons.",
        "REWARD: 300 EXP; return route; final decision recorded.",
        "MQ-14 - Return to Hero's Overlook",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 9-10. Quest giver: Chosen companion.",
        "Author: Escort the Crown to the stone table while allies hold the closing roads.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Three escalating encounters selected from unresolved regional enemies.",
        "REWARD: 300 EXP; all recruited factions added to War Score.",
        "MQ-15 - The Crown of Ash",
        "Quest Journal: Recommended level: Level 10. Quest giver: Final quest.",
        "Author: Defeat the Herald, resolve the Contract phase, confront the Ash form, and choose one of the seven endings.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: The Herald, summoned Greater Demons, Vharruk's three phases.",
        "REWARD: Campaign ending; epilogue based on choices, allies, Ash Clock, and corruption.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - HERO'S OVERLOOK",
        "SQ-HO-01 - The Fifth Shadow",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Brother Aldwyn.",
        "Author: At sunset, a fifth shadow appears between the four statues. Follow it beneath the overlook and recover a bronze nameplate before three Phantoms erase its inscription.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: 3 Phantoms; optional Wraith if the inscription is read aloud.",
        "REWARD: 80 EXP; Fifth Hero clue; +1 trust_aldwyn or +1 suspicion.",
        "SQ-HO-02 - Ash in the Well",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Caretaker Mara.",
        "Author: The village well tastes of smoke. Descend through an old maintenance tunnel, destroy the Slimes feeding on corrupted ash, and purify the spring.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: 3 Slimes and 1 Great Slime.",
        "REWARD: 100 EXP; 2 healing supplies; villagers aid the finale.",
        "SQ-HO-03 - Four Names for the Dead",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Families of missing adventurers.",
        "Author: Find four abandoned Guild tokens along the old road and return them to their families. The last token is carried by a Skeleton Knight who still remembers its owner.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Skeleton group; mercy option for the Knight.",
        "REWARD: 90 EXP; memorial charm; companion loyalty +1.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - MISTHAVEN PORT",
        "SQ-MP-01 - The Lighthouse Below",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Captain Odessa Vray.",
        "Author: The lighthouse beam is being copied beneath the harbor, guiding ships onto hidden rocks. Dive into the flooded foundation, disable the false beacon, and learn who paid for it.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Slimes in flooded chambers; Wraith keeper.",
        "REWARD: 110 EXP; Odessa loyalty +1; fleet route clue.",
        "SQ-MP-02 - Nine Rings, No Champion",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Arena Master Kael.",
        "Author: A Hobgoblin challenger has defeated every Guild fighter without killing anyone. Discover that he seeks protection from Kregg's enemies, then fight, recruit, or expose him.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Optional Hobgoblin duel; Guild enforcers if protected.",
        "REWARD: 100 EXP; arena reputation; Hobgoblin scout ally.",
        "SQ-MP-03 - Lira's Forbidden Chapter",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Lira Sunstroke.",
        "Author: Recover a missing grimoire page from the restricted archive before its unfinished spell summons a Dread Wraith.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Animated books, Phantoms, ritual timer.",
        "REWARD: 130 EXP; Lira loyalty +1; arcane item.",
        "SQ-MP-04 - The Price of Passage",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Dockworkers' Union.",
        "Author: The Guild has seized medicine as \"expedition supplies.\" Decide whether to expose the order, steal the crates, or negotiate their release.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Can be completed without combat; otherwise Guild guards.",
        "REWARD: 90 EXP; medicine for Oakheaven; Corvane evidence.",
        "SQ-MP-05 - A Ship with Two Names",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Captain Odessa Vray.",
        "Author: Odessa's ship appears in the registry under the name of a vessel that sank seven years ago. Search the wreck and recover the original captain's log.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Drowned Phantoms and one Great Chimera near the wreck.",
        "REWARD: 150 EXP; Odessa loyalty +2; Odessa's fleet available later.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - WHISPERING WOODS",
        "SQ-WW-01 - Roots That Speak",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Sil'Vaneth.",
        "Author: Three heart-tree roots repeat the voices of lost travelers. Enter their memories, identify the real call for help, and free the trapped Elf scout.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Phantoms; false-memory puzzles.",
        "REWARD: 120 EXP; Elf scout ally; forest shortcut.",
        "SQ-WW-02 - The Goblin Who Planted Flowers",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Pip Moss-Ear.",
        "Author: A Goblin herbalist is blamed for poisoned flowers, but the poison comes from a corrupted Great Slime. Choose whether to protect Pip from hunters.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Great Slime; optional conflict with hunters.",
        "REWARD: 100 EXP; antidotes; Pip becomes a merchant.",
        "SQ-WW-03 - Moonlight Without a Moon",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Sil'Vaneth.",
        "Author: The forest's moonwell has gone dark. Carry a living flame through Wraith territory without letting it be extinguished.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Two Wraith ambushes; movement challenge.",
        "REWARD: 140 EXP; moonwell blessing; corruption -1.",
        "SQ-WW-04 - The Dread Wraith's Name",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: The forgotten Elf scout.",
        "Author: Collect three memory leaves and speak the Wraith's mortal name. Destroying it is faster; restoring it reveals the Fifth Hero.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Dread Wraith boss or ritual resolution.",
        "REWARD: 170 EXP; traitor clue; Sil'Vaneth loyalty +1.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - ASHTONIA",
        "SQ-AS-01 - Names in the Furnace",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Mother Sereh.",
        "Author: Demons have carved the names of living Orcs into cooling iron. Break the plates before the volcano's next pulse binds those people to the seal.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Demons and one Greater Demon smith.",
        "REWARD: 130 EXP; Mother Sereh loyalty +1; fire resistance supply.",
        "SQ-AS-02 - The Last Clan Drum",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Orc refugee Dorga.",
        "Author: Recover a ceremonial drum from a lava-cut shrine. Its rhythm keeps lesser Demons from approaching, but sounding it also alerts Karnyx.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Demon packs; timed escape.",
        "REWARD: 120 EXP; safe camp in Ashtonia; War Score +1 if preserved.",
        "SQ-AS-03 - A Bargain with No Signature",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Bound Demon Irix.",
        "Author: A lesser Demon claims it was forced into Vharruk's service without signing the contract. Find its true name and decide whether to free, banish, or recruit it as an informant.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Ritual encounter; Greater Demon jailer.",
        "REWARD: 150 EXP; hidden gate information; corruption varies by choice.",
        "SQ-AS-04 - The Ember That Refused",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Mother Sereh.",
        "Author: An ember from the original sealing still burns beneath the shrine. Protect it from a Chimera drawn to its magic and carry it to Hero's Overlook.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Chimera boss.",
        "REWARD: 170 EXP; Sealing Ember; advantage in final Phase Three.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - OAKHEAVEN",
        "SQ-OH-01 - The Mill Race",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Mirelle Ashcroft.",
        "Author: Slimes have blocked the mill channel, stopping the only clean water source. Clear the channel without destroying the old floodgate.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Slimes and one King Slime if Ash Clock is 4+.",
        "REWARD: 110 EXP; clean water; militia health +1.",
        "SQ-OH-02 - Kregg's Stolen Banner",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Kregg the Sundered.",
        "Author: A Demon patrol stole Kregg's banner to provoke Goblins into attacking the town. Recover it and reveal the deception.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Hobgoblins under possession; Demons.",
        "REWARD: 130 EXP; Kregg loyalty +1; goblin alliance route.",
        "SQ-OH-03 - Eleven Empty Beds",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Mirelle Ashcroft.",
        "Author: Eleven townsfolk vanish every night and return at dawn with no memory. Follow them into the orchard and break the possession circle.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Phantoms and a Greater Demon ritualist.",
        "REWARD: 150 EXP; civilians restored; Ash Clock does not advance after resting here.",
        "SQ-OH-04 - The Mayor's Real Voice",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Former clerk Tomas.",
        "Author: Find recordings hidden in the town hall proving when the mayor was possessed. The evidence can convince frightened townsfolk to cooperate.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Possessed guards; stealth or non-lethal route.",
        "REWARD: 100 EXP; easier Oakheaven climax; civilian losses reduced.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - THE BONE PEAKS",
        "SQ-BP-01 - A Knight's Last Order",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Ser Halbrecht.",
        "Author: Recover the command seal of Halbrecht's company and release three Skeleton Knights still patrolling a battle that ended centuries ago.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Skeleton Knights; mercy ritual available.",
        "REWARD: 140 EXP; Halbrecht loyalty +1; undead passage.",
        "SQ-BP-02 - The Troll King's Challenge",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Grommash-Vurr.",
        "Author: Complete three trials - endurance, courage, and mercy - to earn the right to challenge the Troll King without fighting his entire warband.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Warrior Troll trial fights.",
        "REWARD: 160 EXP; honorable duel; potential troll alliance.",
        "SQ-BP-03 - Seven Cold Shrines",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Echo of Nerath-Dur.",
        "Author: Relight seven shrines across Karag-Dur while the Lich's curse sends stronger undead after each flame.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Skeletons, Skeleton Knights, final Wraith.",
        "REWARD: 180 EXP; Lich weakened; corruption -1.",
        "SQ-BP-04 - The Forge Remembers",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Dwarven ancestor stone.",
        "Author: Recover three forge tools from collapsed halls and repair the mechanism that can later reforge the Crown.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Trolls, traps, Great Slime in the cooling cistern.",
        "REWARD: 170 EXP; Karag-Dur forge activated.",
        "SQ-BP-05 - Silence Has Teeth",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Bram Ironjaw.",
        "Author: The unnatural silence is created by a Great Chimera feeding on sound. Track it by vibration and prevent it from consuming Karag-Dur's final lament.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Great Chimera boss.",
        "REWARD: 190 EXP; Bram loyalty +1; sonic protection item.",
        "SIDE QUESTS - DARKSTORM KEEP",
        "SQ-DK-01 - Prisoners of the Seventh Year",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Whisper from the walls.",
        "Author: Find adventurers kept inside magical portraits, defeat the Wraith curators, and choose which memory each prisoner may keep when freed.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Wraiths and one Dread Wraith.",
        "REWARD: 190 EXP; two survivors join the final defense.",
        "SQ-DK-02 - The Chimera's Three Hearts",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Divine Chimera.",
        "Author: Recover the three heart-seals removed by Vharruk. The beast can be defeated for its power or restored as an ally.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Three Great Chimera aspects.",
        "REWARD: 220 EXP; Divine Chimera ally or legendary material.",
        "SQ-DK-03 - Karnyx's Debt",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Karnyx.",
        "Author: Destroy the ledger that binds Karnyx and the Greater Demons to Vharruk. Mercy weakens the enemy army more than simply defeating Karnyx.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Greater Demons; optional Karnyx boss.",
        "REWARD: 210 EXP; Gate of Fire weakened; War Score +1 through truce.",
        "SQ-DK-04 - The Statue That Never Was",
        "Quest Journal: Quest giver: Fellowship echo.",
        "Author: Collect four fragments of the erased fifth statue and assemble them in the Vault. The completed image proves the traitor's identity.",
        "GAME: ENCOUNTERS: Echo fights mirroring the four original heroes.",
        "REWARD: 230 EXP; decisive traitor evidence; special dialogue in MQ-12.",
        "Quest Completion Rules",
        "Author: A quest remains active until its narrative result is known. Failure changes the world rather than deleting progress. A failed rescue can create a later revenge quest; a spared monster can return as an ally; an unfinished regional quest may strengthen one of Darkstorm Keep's gates.",
        "IMPLEMENTATION RULES",
        "Main Quest completed: grant listed EXP and update the story flag.",
        "Side Quest completed: grant listed EXP, reward, and relationship changes.",
        "Combat encounter completed: grant EXP according to the strongest enemy tier plus objective bonuses.",
        "Non-combat solution: grant the same base EXP as combat when the danger is resolved permanently.",
        "Failed objective: grant 40% of quest EXP if the story continues with a meaningful consequence.",
        "Level-up: restore basic resources, grant 3 Skill Points, and display newly eligible quests.",
        "APPENDIX A - OPTIONAL GAMEPLAY TEXT",
        "Ash Clock Messages",
        "GAME: ASH CLOCK 0-3 - The ash is a warning. Roads remain open and hope travels faster than fear.",
        "GAME: ASH CLOCK 4 - Oakheaven falls into panic. Refugees crowd the roads to Misthaven.",
        "GAME: ASH CLOCK 7 - Greater Demons roam openly. Every journey gains a dangerous encounter.",
        "GAME: ASH CLOCK 10 - The storm moves. Vharruk emerges early. The finale begins immediately.",
        "Level-Up Message",
        "GAME: LEVEL UP! Your maximum resources are restored. You receive 3 Skill Points. Check the separate Skill Tree interface to unlock an eligible skill.",
        "Reusable Failure Lines",
        "Author: A failed check should move the story forward with a cost, never stop it completely.",
        "Author: You succeed too late. The way opens, but the Ash Clock advances.",
        "Author: The plan works, though something valuable is left behind.",
        "Author: Your companion completes what you began, and remembers that you needed help.",
        "Author: The enemy withdraws rather than falls. It will return with knowledge of your methods.",
        "Author: The truth is revealed, but to the wrong witness.",
        "End of Script",
        "Author: The Crown of Ash is ready to be told. The player decides whether it becomes a story about victory, truth, responsibility, or the price of choosing for others.",
    };
}
